From 52ed898034bdd8fc798ed11840d175c0a24a0ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:27:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Netplay: give the host its own team back when the room closes

A guest's submitted team is written into the host's socket-3 save, and
it stayed there: the next solo boot used the guest's Pokemon, and so did
the next guest who submitted nothing -- they would battle with a
stranger's team without ever being told. Field-confirmed after a session
where the opponent's imported team carried into the following one.

The first injection of a session now stashes the host's own save beside
it, and closing the room restores that stash. Only the first injection
stashes, so a second submission cannot overwrite the host's copy with
the first guest's team, and a room where nobody submitted leaves nothing
behind to restore. The restore rides the same NetPlayUI hop the
injection uses, so it works on desktop and Android alike.
